{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire","id":1527662,"title":"Progressive Policies are pro.....vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-31T13:15:37-08:00","id":1527662,"title":"Progressive Policies are pro.....vampire?","content":"A recent discussion with a player about how vampires would influence mortal society ended up leading to a strange realization about which side of the aisle they would lend their influence to. Usually vampires are seen as the wealthy elite who control society from the shadows for their own amusement or gain, consuming the lives of the common man to sate their hunger for power, blood, and money. As such most people I have spoken to about this default to the assumption that vampires would back only conservative policies. But when you take examples of real world policies and apply them to vampiric interests, conservative policies don't help vampires much if at all.<br /> <br /> Vampiric interests being the ability to keep themselves hidden, the ability to feed, maintain safety/security, and the ability to acquire &amp; maintain wealth.<br /> <br /> Progressive examples we came up with:<ul><li>Light pollution is a problem so we should have fewer street lamps, the reduction will also mean less energy used every night. Environmental policy which makes hunting easier for vampires.</li> <li>The police are corrupt and fascist, thus they should be defunded. Political policy which means vampires can act up with much less chance of cops being able to respond or effectively patrol areas.</li> <li>Gun violence is a problem; thus second amendment rights should be suspended and concealed carry permits are restricted. Much less likely that prey will be armed, hunters will have a much harder time acquiring weapons or running around with them.</li> <li>People who are arrested for a crime should be given mental health screening to make sure they get the help they need. A policy which allows anyone charged with a crime to bypass the normal criminal legal system and be put in a mental health facility without trial. Then a ghoul doctor can give a false diagnosis or a vampire with Dominate or Dementation can produce mental illness to ensure the person is locked up.</li> <li>Lobby for family court to favor single parent households over nuclear families. The less stable of a home life children have, the greater the chances of them being somewhat broken in adulthood. This means a greater number of people who can disappear and have no one to come look for them. This means more feeding options and less trouble when embracing replacements.</li> <li>Using social media ties to push alternative lifestyles as normal. A vampire with a couple ghouls with the Herd in tow looks remarkably similar to a polycule out on the town.</li> <li>By pushing single parent households and non-traditional relationship models, traditional religions and their beliefs are seen as bigoted and backwards. This means fewer and fewer people believe. This weakens the power of the various churches and makes True Faith even more rare to encounter.</li> <li>Open boarders' policy on migration means large swaths of undocumented immigrants who can be food, followers, or pawns without trace.</li> <li>Reduce the requirements for graduation from high school so that you don't need to be proficient in math, reading, writing, history, or science in order to graduate. Theoretically this reduces the burden on people of color when it comes to graduation, I honestly don't get the logic. But as far as vampires are concerned, an uneducated humanity is far easier to control. Alternatively those mortals who teach themselves and rise to the top have the sort of skills and mindset required to be potential new embrace material.</li> <li>Back policies which assist homeless individuals without actually solving the homeless issue. This creates a readymade scape goat for when anything crazy happens and enough &quot;political noise&quot; that vampire behavior is hidden from public view.</li> </ul><br /> The conservative examples we came up with:<ul><li>Increased development of rural land surrounding cities to keep shifters further and further away.</li> <li>Reduced taxes on businesses, though to be fair conservative and progressive business owners bellyache about this equally in my opinion.</li> <li>Removal of inheritance taxes, every time a vampire has to fake their death and leave everything to themselves, it costs them a chunk of resources.</li> </ul><br /> An interesting example of a policy that could go either way depending on how you look at it:<br /> <br /> Public surveillance systems in cities. Generally conservatives are against such systems and progressives are for such systems. But at the current time facial identification software is far more accurate at recognizing people of with pale skin than people of color. This makes the progressives instantly switch sides on the topic and see it as a tool of oppression. <br /> <br /> The catch is that Facial ID systems would be a default masquerade threat for all vampires regardless of how much easier it would be to track and control mortals. Though since all vampires other than assamites grow more pale, then the current software would actually be very good at IDing cainites. So this policy can be pushed by pretty much any camp.<br /> <br /> <br /> So what sort of policies have you used in your games to push a vampire agenda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":10},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T14:14:59-08:00","id":1527664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire#post1527662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A recent discussion with a player about how vampires would influence mortal society ended up leading to a strange realization about which side of the aisle they would lend their influence to. Usually vampires are seen as the wealthy elite who control society from the shadows for their own amusement or gain, consuming the lives of the common man to sate their hunger for power, blood, and money. As such most people I have spoken to about this default to the assumption that vampires would back only conservative policies. But when you take examples of real world policies and apply them to vampiric interests, conservative policies don't help vampires much if at all.<br /> <br /> Vampiric interests being the ability to keep themselves hidden, the ability to feed, maintain safety/security, and the ability to acquire &amp; maintain wealth.<br /> <br /> Progressive examples we came up with:<br /> <br /> Light pollution is a problem so we should have fewer street lamps, the reduction will also mean less energy used every night. Environmental policy which makes hunting easier for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that could also aid Garou and/or Fera, possibly even in hunting vampires since the licks would flock to the dark areas, and well, probably not suspect that they're being watched. A small sliver of opportunity for SI with night vision, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The police are corrupt and fascist, thus they should be defunded. Political policy which means vampires can act up with much less chance of cops being able to respond or effectively patrol areas. </div> </div> </div>Like they did before? Vampires are typically one of the reasons that the cops are corrupt and fascist. I don't buy this one as a vampire-friendly one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gun violence is a problem; thus second amendment rights should be suspended and concealed carry permits are restricted. Much less likely that prey will be armed, hunters will have a much harder time acquiring weapons or running around with them. </div> </div> </div>...nor this one. Vampires have very little to fear from standard guns unless they're like .50 cal or up. Hairspray and a lighter are arguably more threatening to most licks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People who are arrested for a crime should be given mental health screening to make sure they get the help they need. A policy which allows anyone charged with a crime to bypass the normal criminal legal system and be put in a mental health facility without trial. Then a ghoul doctor can give a false diagnosis or a vampire with Dominate or Dementation can produce mental illness to ensure the person is locked up. </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure this is &quot;progressive&quot; as such, but I suppose that the SI could also use it to get their people out of trouble. &quot;He's convinced that vampires exist, he's clearly lost it. Now look away while we do some other legal shenanigans to shuffle him out of any custody and back into a quiet desk job.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lobby for family court to favor single parent households over nuclear families. The less stable of a home life children have, the greater the chances of them being somewhat broken in adulthood. This means a greater number of people who can disappear and have no one to come look for them. This means more feeding options and less trouble when embracing replacements. </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced that's even a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using social media ties to push alternative lifestyles as normal. A vampire with a couple ghouls with the Herd in tow looks remarkably similar to a polycule out on the town. </div> </div> </div>If the polycule is completely dysfunctional, maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By pushing single parent households and non-traditional relationship models, traditional religions and their beliefs are seen as bigoted and backwards. This means fewer and fewer people believe. This weakens the power of the various churches and makes True Faith even more rare to encounter. </div> </div> </div>That's not a policy, that's just the traditional side throwing tantrums and looking less and less reasonable as a consequence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Open boarders' policy on migration means large swaths of undocumented immigrants who can be food, followers, or pawns without trace. </div> </div> </div>If the policy were actually progressive they could seek asylum and documentation and not be classified as illegal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reduce the requirements for graduation from high school so that you don't need to be proficient in math, reading, writing, history, or science in order to graduate. Theoretically this reduces the burden on people of color when it comes to graduation, I honestly don't get the logic. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound very easy to get when you put it that way, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But as far as vampires are concerned, an uneducated humanity is far easier to control. Alternatively those mortals who teach themselves and rise to the top have the sort of skills and mindset required to be potential new embrace material. </div> </div> </div>That's getting into some very suspect chains of logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back policies which <b>assist homeless individuals without actually solving the homeless issue</b>. This creates a readymade scape goat for when anything crazy happens and enough &quot;political noise&quot; that vampire behavior is hidden from public view. </div> </div> </div>That's... also not very progressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what sort of policies have you used in your games to push a vampire agenda? </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure how much further licks could push things without tipping their hands about their existence. It's more like they find these things out after the fact and then support them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T14:21:06-08:00","id":1527665,"title":"","content":"Eh, big deal. Ain\u2019t the first time would-be progressive politics screwed up in places they missed looking or deliberately buried for sake of their Greater Good; a Horror/Fantasy equivalent isn\u2019t hard to imagine from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T15:46:17-08:00","id":1527669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527664#post1527664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...nor this one. Vampires have very little to fear from standard guns unless they're like .50 cal or up. Hairspray and a lighter are arguably more threatening to most licks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen TPKs with nothing larger than 7.62 and 9mm being used. Hairspray has a range of a couple of feet to set anything on fire. Are you using some custom rules for combat or do you play in games that are expressly combat tank builds? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527664#post1527664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure this is &quot;progressive&quot; as such, but I suppose that the SI could also use it to get their people out of trouble. &quot;He's convinced that vampires exist, he's clearly lost it. Now look away while we do some other legal shenanigans to shuffle him out of any custody and back into a quiet desk job.&quot;\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The key thing is to avoid the term &quot;vampire&quot; or anything related to it that would alert the SI or other Hunters in the first place. A hunter that reads the headline &quot;boarding school shooter trying to hunt vampires&quot; will have a different reaction than reading &quot;boarding school shooter ranting about immoral yogurt being served at lunch&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T17:08:59-08:00","id":1527671,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure that a lot of the things listed are &quot;progressive policies&quot; let alone that they would help vampires.<br /> <br /> Like take immigration -<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire#post1527662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open boarders' policy on migration means large swaths of undocumented immigrants who can be food, followers, or pawns without trace.So what sort of policies have you used in your games to push a vampire agenda?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires would absolutely prefer the current system, with people who are illegally trafficked into the country, and who are too afraid to contact the police or media or anyone else when they're victims of crime (or vampire attacks) because of fear of being deported. One of the ideas among the pro-immigration crowd is that by allowing more people to come in legally who would otherwise try to come in illegally, that these immigrants will be documented, and that means they could (for example) safely contact the police or other groups when they're victims of crimes.<br /> <br /> That's the absolute last thing vampires would want to see. It's much easier to attack someone or feed on them or make them &quot;disappear&quot; if that person was trafficked into the country since there's no documentation that they even exist to begin with and if they tried to go to the police they'd likely be deported. The goal of pro-immigration policies is to bring people out of the shadows, and that's where vampires prefer their victims to be.<br /> <br /> Or like with guns, vampires aren't running around dragging random people off the street to eat. Most vampires have herds or do their feeding in places like clubs or other social venues. So guns and an armed population are kind of irrelevant to vampire feeding, overall. In fact I imagine most vampires probably prefer having access to legal weapons, at least for their ghouls, bodyguards, etc. So I doubt vampires tend towards gun-control since fewer guns doesn't really benefit them. Plus more guns = more violence in general, which probably suits most vampires, since that sort of instability means more potential targets for feeding, more crime, more gangs, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-01-2024, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T17:42:25-08:00","id":1527672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527669#post1527669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have seen TPKs with nothing larger than 7.62 and 9mm being used. Hairspray has a range of a couple of feet to set anything on fire. Are you using some custom rules for combat or do you play in games that are expressly combat tank builds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't vampires suffer gun damage as bashing and halve it? That's the basis of my pressing X to doubt here. Improvised incendiaries deal agg and potentially cause Red Fear. They literally fear them more than guns because fire bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The key thing is to avoid the term &quot;vampire&quot; or anything related to it that would alert the SI or other Hunters in the first place. A hunter that reads the headline &quot;boarding school shooter trying to hunt vampires&quot; will have a different reaction than reading &quot;boarding school shooter ranting about immoral yogurt being served at lunch&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, any method gets stale and predictable if you use it long enough, and it's not like vampires causing people to become mentally unstable is rare knowledge, in the WoD or not, courtesy of Bram Stoker's book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T19:37:23-08:00","id":1527675,"title":"","content":"Just a few things I thought about these points:<br /> <br /> Firstly the issue of the police, I think it is more appropriate for them to control them and if they are corrupt, they will let anything through with the right incentive and they can still look after the herd and be a scapegoat for popular anger.<br /> <br /> Guns, I don't think it would make that much of a difference unless they banned it completely, which would lead to revolt. You can do it in the game, but I think it's unnecessary, as hunters could still obtain it by other means and the end result would be the same in game.<br /> <br /> As for hospitals, I think it's easier for them to buy a hospital to use as a base, catch people off the street and lock them up like crazy using discipline, better than risking changing the law by having to catch aggressive criminals.<br /> <br /> Using social media... I think it would work at first, but won't it become another warning for hunters?<br /> <br /> As for taxes in general, if the vampires control the economy don't those taxes already come back to them? other than leaving the politicians happy by taking what they can.<br /> <br /> If Facil ID systems are a problem for them, they could make contraptions and use in their favor, except in the V5 scenerio. In game, I don't know, ST could use or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T20:04:00-08:00","id":1527676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527672#post1527672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't vampires suffer gun damage as bashing and halve it? That's the basis of my pressing X to doubt here. Improvised incendiaries deal agg and potentially cause Red Fear. They literally fear them more than guns because fire bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>With V20 and earlier versions, vampires treat generic ammunition as bashing rather than lethal, thus able to use their full stamina rating to soak. A quick check doesn't immediately bring up a &quot;half it&quot; mechanic. But if this is a V5 thing, I wouldn't know about it.<br /> <br /> Though I would also point out that &quot;headshots&quot; count as lethal rather than bashing when using melee weapons, so I have heard arguements about using the same rule for firearms headshots.<br /> <br /> So the average non-combat optimized character will only have 2 dots in stamina, which can only at best half the damage of a generic 9mm bullet with a damage of 4 or less in the case of a 7.62 which would be an assault rifle round with a damage of 7.<br /> <br /> I keep bringing up the &quot;generic&quot; aspect of ammunition because the WoD Combat supplement gave additional rules for ammunition types, so a basic Ak-47 with what amounts to ball ammo is a considerably different threat than the same gun loaded with exclusively tracer ammunition, which is phosphorus based, which bumps it up to lethal or aggravated, on top of the aiming bonus, depending on how much your ST knows about guns.<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned TPKs were just run of the mill ammo, rather than anything fancy. But the coterie were not combat optimized nor wearing anything heavier than leather jackets.<br /> <br /> As for the fire causing fear issue, that is a matter of situation. Plenty of firearms produce a small gout of flame when firing, but there isn't rules for that freaking vampires out. A candle flame can theoretically induce a fear response but there has to be some context of danger, otherwise vampires couldn't enter cities or anyones home after dark before the proliferation of the electric light bulb, because they would automatically run screaming off into the night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T23:05:14-08:00","id":1527681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527676#post1527676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With V20 and earlier versions, vampires treat generic ammunition as bashing rather than lethal, thus able to use their full stamina rating to soak. A quick check doesn't immediately bring up a &quot;half it&quot; mechanic. But if this is a V5 thing, I wouldn't know about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 page 281, firearms vs. vampires are bashing. V20 pg 285, all bashing damage to Kindred is halved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I would also point out that &quot;headshots&quot; count as lethal rather than bashing when using melee weapons, so I have heard arguements about using the same rule for firearms headshots. </div> </div> </div>This is also cited as an option on page 281.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the average non-combat optimized character will only have 2 dots in stamina, which can only at best half the damage of a generic 9mm bullet with a damage of 4 or less in the case of a 7.62 which would be an assault rifle round with a damage of 7.<br /> <br /> I keep bringing up the &quot;generic&quot; aspect of ammunition because the WoD Combat supplement gave additional rules for ammunition types, so a basic Ak-47 with what amounts to ball ammo is a considerably different threat than the same gun loaded with exclusively tracer ammunition, which is phosphorus based, which bumps it up to lethal or aggravated, on top of the aiming bonus, depending on how much your ST knows about guns. </div> </div> </div>WoD: Combat isn't really readily compatible with V20. Also, the tracer rounds would need to be up close to be threatening in this capacity unless there was a lot of tinder, dry brush, or other flammable material around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The previously mentioned TPKs were just run of the mill ammo, rather than anything fancy. But the coterie were not combat optimized nor wearing anything heavier than leather jackets. </div> </div> </div>I wonder if there are more misgivings with said group on account of the terrible book layout and organization or because you didn't read all of it. (The last edition before that, Revised, also quite notably had bullets doing bashing and all bashing being halved; it was one of the major noted differences between it and 2e.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the fire causing fear issue, that is a matter of situation. Plenty of firearms produce a small gout of flame when firing, but there isn't rules for that freaking vampires out. A candle flame can theoretically induce a fear response but there has to be some context of danger, otherwise vampires couldn't enter cities or anyones home after dark before the proliferation of the electric light bulb, because they would automatically run screaming off into the night. </div> </div> </div>Fire exploding around you from improvised incendiaries would probably be a bit more threatening than the gun discharge.<br /> <br /> In any case, this is getting a bit off topic, as the military and militarized police don't need to observe gun laws, and are the most likely forces to use those rounds. Must have pissed off an elder something fierce to get them to throw that at the coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T11:10:45-08:00","id":1527699,"title":"","content":"I think the fundamental lesson of vampire is that they are parasites and will turn all policies to their favor. They naturally corrupt and manipulate human institutions and both progressive and conservative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T12:05:51-08:00","id":1527703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527681#post1527681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire exploding around you from improvised incendiaries would probably be a bit more threatening than the gun discharge.</div> </div> </div> </div>A hairspray and flame combo doesn't explode during use, so you wouldn't use improvised explosive rules. Some one using that is about as dangerous at distance greater than five feet as someone turning on a stove.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527681#post1527681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, this is getting a bit off topic, as the military and militarized police don't need to observe gun laws, and are the most likely forces to use those rounds. Must have pissed off an elder something fierce to get them to throw that at the coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the incidents I was referring to the coterie was dealing with civilians. One situation involved a street gang, another involved a survivalist gun nut.<br /> <br /> The gang had received a weapons shipment of ak-47s and despite a small mountain of evidence that they were armed, the coterie decided that kicking in the front door of their house was the best course of action. The shipment was 50 rifles and a bunch of ammo, just having ten rifles open up dropped all but one of the coterie to torpor, and that one was holding on by one health level. He died trying to get back to the haven. Annoyed elders are deadly, but not as deadly as playing ones characters in the &quot;chaotic stupid&quot; alignment. <br /> <br /> As for how compatible WoD Combat is with V20, V20 didn't exist yet when these games happened. The side effect of playing since first edition is that V20 and V5 still feel like the new kids on the block.<br /> <br /> Now getting back to the core of the thread which isn't what you think of the examples, but what policies you have used in your games when vampires adjusted mortal society. So have you done that at all in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:52:09-08:00","id":1527712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527703#post1527703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A hairspray and flame combo doesn't explode during use, so you wouldn't use improvised explosive rules. Some one using that is about as dangerous at distance greater than five feet as someone turning on a stove.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was scratching the surface of possibilities. I did switch to saying improvised incendiaries and not that specific case for a reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the incidents I was referring to the coterie was dealing with civilians. One situation involved a street gang, another involved a survivalist gun nut.<br /> <br /> The gang had received a weapons shipment of ak-47s and despite a small mountain of evidence that they were armed, the coterie decided that kicking in the front door of their house was the best course of action. The shipment was 50 rifles and a bunch of ammo, just having ten rifles open up dropped all but one of the coterie to torpor, and that one was holding on by one health level. He died trying to get back to the haven. Annoyed elders are deadly, but not as deadly as playing ones characters in the &quot;chaotic stupid&quot; alignment.<br /> <br /> As for how compatible WoD Combat is with V20, V20 didn't exist yet when these games happened. The side effect of playing since first edition is that V20 and V5 still feel like the new kids on the block. </div> </div> </div>Then why did you cite V20 and Revised rules in a block with 1e and 2e just a few posts ago? Especially when V20 and Revised been around for a combined length of 26 years now? And why stick with WoD: Combat when you're trying to make vampires want to disarm people when those rules allow unarmed combatants to basically beat vampires to final death just by spending some extra Willpower? (Any maneuver can be made to do &quot;kill damage&quot; this way and people can jump Exalted leaping distances if they have the Jump maneuver! The licks don't stand a chance!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now getting back to the core of the thread which isn't what you think of the examples </div> </div> </div>Okay but they were pretty bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but what policies you have used in your games when vampires adjusted mortal society. So have you done that at all in your games? </div> </div> </div>Vampires have already adjusted mortal society in the WoD. Like, completely. Most progressive policies would probably work against them. They are the asshole.<br /> <br /> That said, I did once have an idea about Hungry Dead that followed the Face of the Gods Dharma using religious freedom in the US as a weapon. Mostly against the Kindred, since that's a thing they would probably do, but it could easily branch out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T03:22:30-08:00","id":1527762,"title":"","content":"I thought that the reason vampires, especially Masquerade vampires, tended to support the establishment was because they are the establishment (metaphorically at least, but also often literally). Brujah definitely support left wing policies as part of their experiments and their ties to academia, but even then conservative Brujah are probably more common than liberal Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Heck some of these policies are things I've seen actual right wing governments enact. Thanks austerity!<br /> <br /> I think the others have gone over why most of these ideas aren't so hot, but I have issues with two:<br /> <br /> I've known a few people who might squeak out a point of True Faith and they have been everywhere from 'firmly socialist' to 'reactionary', with a trend towards the former only because my social circle does. There's definitely a different view of faith among most left-wingers I know, but that's more it being seen as a personal matter then less faith. I know at least one person who outright refuses to share if they are religious or not, and nobody pries.<br /> <br /> As to polycules pretty much anytime you could use 'we're a polycule' as a disguise you can use 'we're a group of friends' and have no issues. One fewer actually: nobody's going to ask why you're smooching a Nosferatu (idiots, Nossies are great kissers). It makes as much sense as supporting Doctor Who LARPs to explain the Venture's out of date clothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T07:44:02-08:00","id":1527771,"title":"","content":"My inclination is that vampires have influence over politics just like real world powerful people have influence over politics - they aren't usually partisan, they control both sides of the aisle and make it so that no matter which party of politician wins, they do too. There are exceptions of course. Sometime a actual anti-establishment candidate wins and sometimes you get a billionaire that is actually really partisan.<br /> <br /> So vampires influence both (or all in nations with more major parties) and only their versions of right or left are allowed to win. Whether it's a Republican or a Democrat, they are still going to ultimately serve a blood sucker before the American people. Just like in real life, just more literally.<br /> <br /> Though one issue that often comes up is the idea that vampires would want to influence politics to make things worse. More crime, more poverty, more corruption, and so on. This leads left leaning people to think that vampires would support right leaning politics and for right leaning people to think that vampires support left leaning politics. I don't think that this is necessarily true though.<br /> <br /> Sure, a pack of Sabbat or a bunch of Anarch neonates might like it if there were more crime and poverty so that they could more easily get away with crimes. But are those the kinds of vampires who are going to be deciding who becomes the mayor or governor? No, certainly not. Camarilla elders, especially Ventrue, Toreador, and Tremere are going to be pulling the string there. These kinds of vampires aren't going to be on the streets committing crimes, murdering random homeless people, and other such nonsense. Those vampires are going to establish a safe and reliable method of feeding that doesn't involve random violence. Having a herd, buying from slaughter houses, getting blood from hospitals, and so on. Even relatively young vampires of less affluent Clans are unlikely to frequently engage in random crimes, at least if they're smart. By the time you become an influential elder you're never going to be getting your hands dirty like that nor would you tolerate your allies or servants doing that either.<br /> <br /> So would these sorts of vampires want a bunch of crime, homelessness, corruption, and general chaos? I would say no. They want happy contented people who go to work, take care of their responsibilities, obey the law, and sit down in front of their TV/computer to zone out and don't ask questions or get too involved. Trouble like poverty and crime makes people pay attention, that isn't good for vampires. Shepherds don't want vicious sheep that are hungry and fighting all the time so that they are too distracted to notice humans slaughtering them. They want peaceful docile sheep that go where they are told. Of course, vampires do want corruption in that they are going to want police and politicians to do what the vampiric rulers want, they aren't going to want those police and politicians breaking laws and taking bribes all the time. These servants should generally be law abiding except in those rare cases when their true vampires call on special favors.<br /> <br /> On a personal level, I think that there might be a tendency for vampires to lean towards the right on certain issues, being that most of them were born and raised long ago when society's values were more conservative. Once vampires get to the level of significantly influencing politics, those personal feeling probably wont be a major factor.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:57:46-07:00","id":1536957,"title":"","content":"I don't know where your opinion is coming from, but vampires are eternally locked in stasis, unchanged from the moment they were Embraced. They are the literal embodiment of &quot;Conservatism,&quot; i.e., &quot;Stasis.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:49:05-07:00","id":1537075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1536957#post1536957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where your opinion is coming from, but vampires are eternally locked in stasis, unchanged from the moment they were Embraced. They are the literal embodiment of &quot;Conservatism,&quot; i.e., &quot;Stasis.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those concepts that the writers and the fans can never seem to make up their minds about.<br /> <br /> Because if vampires are as unchanging as you say, then they have no capacity to adjust, adapt, or learn new things. A vampire who was embraced during the roman empire will never learn a new language, never learn how to drive a car, never use weapons that aren't a sword and shield, they will never accept that slavery isn't an answer, they believe that anyone who isn't of Greek or Roman descent is automatically a barbarian, etc.<br /> <br /> This fundamentally means that XP as a system doesn't work because a vampire is frozen at the time of undeath, thus unable to uprade stats. They can't choose new paths of enlightenment because they always start out as path of humanity. Furthermore, let us not forget that the Gangrel clan weakness changes them over time, the nosferatu clan weakness changes them at the point of the embrace, the Assamite clan attribute means they get darker as they age, and the entire discipline of Vicissitude is based around the concept of making permanent changes to ones form. Never mind the fact that all the paths and rituals of blood magic that were created by vampires couldn't exist.<br /> <br /> Writing that Vampires are frozen in thinking and in their &quot;time&quot; is arguably more a projection of the writer hating on older and more experienced individuals, without actually having a reason to do so. Everything in the WoD is theoretically about being able to adapt and survive, but if one is frozen in stasis, then you by definition can't adapt or create new tactics.<br /> <br /> Other than a mention from Ann Rice, I don't think most other vampire media runs with the idea that vampires are unchanging psychologically as a function of vampiric existence, rather it is a side effect of long-term existence where you have seen everything to the point where you can guess what will happen next because the patterns are so boringly repetitive.<br /> <br /> As a side note, where do you get the absurd notion that Conservatism somehow equals stasis? Conservatism is more akin to &quot;if it ain't broke, don't fix it&quot;. Traditional methods work until they don't and then they get updated, but the core values remain largely the same. While Progressivism is constantly chasing what could be possible, but to quote Ian Malcolm &quot;your scientists were so focused on whether or not if they could, they never stopped to consider if they should&quot;. Thus revolutions and other progressions in society never know when to stop and often turn in on themselves once they run out of other enemies to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T07:56:14-07:00","id":1537084,"title":"","content":"Elders and ancients maybe are stubborn and hold onto traditions that hold meaning for them, but they are not static and do adapt to the changing times if for nothing else to see how it benefits them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T11:56:10-07:00","id":1537095,"title":"","content":"I assume with the &quot;punk&quot; element emphasized that vampire elders have the exact same policies as billionaires and protecting themselves from anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T12:09:58-07:00","id":1537098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537095#post1537095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume with the &quot;punk&quot; element emphasized that vampire elders have the exact same policies as billionaires and protecting themselves from anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tend to agree with that being part of it, but that behavior is also found in millionaires and older individuals who have worked for something and achieved it and thus wish to protect it.<br /> <br /> Though I would also point out that it is exceedingly rare for those who gain power/money/influence to not immediately turn around and take on the same attributes and follow the same actions now that they have &quot;made it&quot;. The BLM activists who spent donated money for personal mansions rather than helping black businesses or ensuring grocery stores exist in black neighborhoods that are now food deserts are a depressing recent example.<br /> <br /> It's a said commentary when VtM and WoD is less depressing than the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T13:30:07-07:00","id":1537110,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of a statement from Mick \u201cMankind\u201d Foley from his Foley is Good book and states how the real world can be more fake then professional wrestling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T16:38:08-07:00","id":1537120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537110#post1537110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of a statement from Mick \u201cMankind\u201d Foley from his Foley is Good book and states how the real world can be more fake then professional wrestling.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I used to watch wrestling as a kid, I had to think for a minute and realized that &quot;Mankind&quot; was a new guy that showed up after I stopped watching. He debuted in 1996.... for the record all you whippersnappers need get off my lawn.<br /> <br /> grumble grumble grumble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T17:00:46-07:00","id":1537122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1527676#post1527676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With V20 and earlier versions, vampires treat generic ammunition as bashing rather than lethal, thus able to use their full stamina rating to soak. A quick check doesn't immediately bring up a &quot;half it&quot; mechanic. But if this is a V5 thing, I wouldn't know about it.. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true, vampires suffer only bashing-damage from gunshots, there are very few vampires that enjoy getting shot. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T17:50:39-07:00","id":1537124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537110#post1537110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of a statement from Mick \u201cMankind\u201d Foley from his Foley is Good book and states how the real world can be more fake then professional wrestling.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sounds like you're scared, Boulder!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T20:46:50-07:00","id":1537131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1536957#post1536957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where your opinion is coming from, but vampires are eternally locked in stasis, unchanged from the moment they were Embraced. They are the literal embodiment of &quot;Conservatism,&quot; i.e., &quot;Stasis.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that fails for player characters as vampires are pretty solidly divided between the conservative Elders and the radical revolutionary Anarchs. Unless all Anarchs are meant to be youngins that seems like it defeats the purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T03:51:43-07:00","id":1537144,"title":"","content":"Regardless of the logic behind the original post in terms of what counts as progressive, and whether it would help vampires, here's my own take.<br /> <br /> Left wing political initiatives would be to the benefit of a typical vampire, in the sense that they're to the benefit of everyone. A cheap night train; a stranded neonate can get out of Sabbat territory despite their phone being dead, with the coins in their pocket. Easily available shelter, without means testing; a Ventrue ancilla who has been refused shelter by a clanmate (the scandal!) and whose ghoul has gone missing (kidnapped? killed?) can find somewhere to shelter from the sunrise, even if the humiliation of using a shelter for KINE haunts them for decades. Health initiatives to get rid of lead paint and asbestos; healthier herd, better blood.<br /> <br /> There are two complications, however:<br /> <br /> Vampires are not wholly logical creatures. The Camarilla is a Conservative organization, being a Kindred is seen as a Conservative calling, much like organized crime. Think Sopranos, Ozark. &quot;This is not a liberal profession. It is deeply conservative&quot; (in reference to executing a mentally ill man because he is a liability). This can be more a cultural thing than something rational. Look at the power vertical. Look at the traditionalism, the conservative (small c) sensibilities, the decorum. A typical Camarilla Kindred will be more drawn towards Conservative politics simply because it feels familiar, the aesthetic similarities distract them from the benefits left wing politics could have for Kindred.<br /> <br /> In addition to this, there is corruption. Yes, a cheap night train would be good for the neonate on the street. But you're the Ventrue Primogen, and you haven't needed PUBLIC TRANSPORT (ugh) in well over 2 centuries, if ever. In fact the idea that the government might pay to move people around with a subsidized service could be very unnatural to you. You're from a time where if anyone ever needed to go further than their town or village, they'd pay a premium and give up a few days of their life. A random teenager stranded away from their parents being able to get home, rather than being a Sabbat snack, doesn't seem like a natural thing to you, even if it would benefit you. And more to the point, even if you realize it would benefit the Camarilla as a whole... do you care? Do you want to pay tax? Do you want the pax you do pay to be higher? Do you want the Neonates and Ancillae to be having an easier time? Does the welfare of the Kine as a whole matter that much to you, when you're feeding on those who are generally doing okay? And your Ghoul has a lot of influence in the world of corrupt bastards. So do all your business partners. You're making a lot of money off things being the way they are.<br /> <br /> This is where Anarchs come in. Neonates and Fledgelings and even Ancilla are getting crumbs at many tables. Trying to claw back some of the power which is being taken by the Elders, being a punk or a rebel, these are anti-establishment and help to balance things out. While many princes will be supporting a candidate who supports the status quo (this doesn't necessarily mean right wing; there are plenty of purportedly progressive / left wing parties who often have leaders who support keeping things as they are, look at the US and UK for two pretty big examples), there will also be Kindred who are trying to scupper this out of principle or as part of the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Kindred act out of self-interest in many cases, and they won't always understand what is in their best interests, meaning they will at times act selfishly even to their own detriment, or that of their fellow Kindred","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T07:56:41-07:00","id":1537151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537144#post1537144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you want the pax you do pay to be higher?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I've just got to check with my accountant about the pax I owe. Let's see, is it Orion, or OH GOD IT'S CAESTUS!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T15:07:26-07:00","id":1537162,"title":"","content":"The punk definition for conservatism works very well for V:TM.<br /> <br /> &quot;That there must be a group that the law protects but does not bind and a group that the law binds but does not protect.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T12:48:38-07:00","id":1537211,"title":"","content":"Business as usual in other words CTPhipps<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T19:05:54-07:00","id":1537241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537162#post1537162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The punk definition for conservatism works very well for V:TM.<br /> <br /> &quot;That there must be a group that the law protects but does not bind and a group that the law binds but does not protect.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is extremely true for VtM. As far as more elder vampires are concerned, the Laws of the Camarilla should protect elder vampires, but not bind them. Conversely the Laws of the Camarilla should bind younger vampires but not protect them. If a younger vampire insults an elder, and the elder responds by killing the younger vampire, the elder is likely to receive some sort of slap on the wrist as punishment. &quot;Well, that youngster had it coming insulting someone who was born before Columbus ever left Italy. Let that serve as a lesson.&quot; Meanwhile if an elder vampire insults a younger one, and the younger one murders the elder, you can bet that that young vampire is going to face a blood hunt for doing that.<br /> <br /> While post-Anarch Revolt, the Camarilla's system is fairer than the system that used to exist, it's still not anything that could be considered remotely fair or even-handed. <br /> <br /> This also goes to some degree with the idea of mortal laws and vampires. Vampires generally don't feel that they should be bound by mortal laws, but they will absolutely use mortal laws (and law enforcement) to protect themselves from mortals when the need arises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T20:53:04-07:00","id":1537244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537241#post1537241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a younger vampire insults an elder, and the elder responds by killing the younger vampire, the elder is likely to receive some sort of slap on the wrist as punishment. &quot;Well, that youngster had it coming insulting someone who was born before Columbus ever left Italy. Let that serve as a lesson.&quot; Meanwhile if an elder vampire insults a younger one, and the younger one murders the elder, you can bet that that young vampire is going to face a blood hunt for doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this being a common perception, but it would be just as accurate to say that if an Elder got killed by a young upstart, clearly that Elder wasn't worth the blood they fed on. For every Elder that would mourn or try to avenge the death of their contemporary, there are several Elders who don't care one way or the other, and more than a few that breath a sigh of relief because the boons or old deals made are now no longer in play.<br /> <br /> The idea of &quot;fairness&quot; in modern times has lost all connection to the reality of a given situation. If a stupid individual gets into a fight with a smart individual, the smart one is not going to lobotomize themselves so that they two can have an equal fight. A young vampire who picks a fight with an Elder without accounting for the power difference is outright stupid, but so is an Elder who believes themselves untouchable and thus goes about making enemies left and right out of every new vampire.<br /> <br /> I believe the perception that Elders are these non-stop pricks is due not to their age &amp; power, but instead because of bad character writing and storytelling. Elders have survived this long for a reason, yet so many STs have elders be glorified high school lunchroom bullies who are a year or two older and thus have more physical development and more social clout.<br /> <br /> An Elder should either be such a heavy combat build that they don't need to be smart, or they should be acting like Xanatos, where every plan has multiple potential outcomes, but regardless of what happens, the elder benefits. Occasionally you will get an Elder who is both a heavy combat build and a Xanatos clone, but you will almost never find an Elder who does neither of those things well, they just wouldn't survive long enough to become Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T21:00:38-07:00","id":1537245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537244#post1537244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see this being a common perception, but it would be just as accurate to say that if an Elder got killed by a young upstart, clearly that Elder wasn't worth the blood they fed on. For every Elder that would mourn or try to avenge the death of their contemporary, there are several Elders who don't care one way or the other, and more than a few that breath a sigh of relief because the boons or old deals made are now no longer in play.<br /> <br /> The idea of &quot;fairness&quot; in modern times has lost all connection to the reality of a given situation. If a stupid individual gets into a fight with a smart individual, the smart one is not going to lobotomize themselves so that they two can have an equal fight. A young vampire who picks a fight with an Elder without accounting for the power difference is outright stupid, but so is an Elder who believes themselves untouchable and thus goes about making enemies left and right out of every new vampire.<br /> <br /> I believe the perception that Elders are these non-stop pricks is due not to their age &amp; power, but instead because of bad character writing and storytelling. Elders have survived this long for a reason, yet so many STs have elders be glorified high school lunchroom bullies who are a year or two older and thus have more physical development and more social clout.<br /> <br /> An Elder should either be such a heavy combat build that they don't need to be smart, or they should be acting like Xanatos, where every plan has multiple potential outcomes, but regardless of what happens, the elder benefits. Occasionally you will get an Elder who is both a heavy combat build and a Xanatos clone, but you will almost never find an Elder who does neither of those things well, they just wouldn't survive long enough to become Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of animals, humans included, actually have seemingly inborn notions of fairness that they react poorly to if they happen to be violated. Of course, if vampires are vampires and undead mockeries of life, then fuck 'em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T21:05:56-07:00","id":1537247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537162#post1537162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The punk definition for conservatism works very well for V:TM.<br /> <br /> &quot;That there must be a group that the law protects but does not bind and a group that the law binds but does not protect.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say a better definition would be as follows:<br /> <br /> Camarilla: Classical Fascism as defined by Mussolini as &quot;Everything inside the state, nothing outside the state, nothing above the state&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Hedonistic Blood Cult who believe themselves the heroes for fighting against the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: You're not my real parent, you can't tell me what to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem with &quot;punk&quot; is that as a political viewpoint, it doesn't understand anything beyond itself. It is being counter to whatever the current mainstream accepts. Thus &quot;Punk&quot; can easily identify with whatever is fringe at the moment, thus why Traditionalist values were antithetical to punk back in the 80's and 90's and now with all the progressive stuff going on in society these days, wanting a traditional monogamous family unit is considered subversive by some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T21:17:08-07:00","id":1537248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537245#post1537245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of animals, humans included, actually have seemingly inborn notions of fairness that they react poorly to if they happen to be violated. Of course, if vampires are vampires and undead mockeries of life, then fuck 'em.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh, the core issue is what is considered &quot;fair&quot; rather than the existence of fairness being violated.<br /> <br /> Toss two people in a pit, put a knife in the center, state that whichever one is still alive by the end gets to leave. <br /> <br /> They start equidistant from the knife, they are both equally forced into the situation, they are both promised the same prize for achieving victory. That is pretty dang fair in the grand scheme of things, because people understand that bad situations happen and you just have to deal with them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the person who doesn't pay attention to the situation and starts complaining that it is unfair that they are forced to compete... is usually the one who gets stabbed by the one who doesn't have a problem with it. But this too is a fair outcome because the individuals had the freedom of choice for what they wanted to prioritize, their philosophical integrity or their continued survival.<br /> <br /> Also I would be willing to bet that most animals that care about &quot;fairness&quot; are also domesticated, meaning their lives are sheltered from the harsher realities of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T22:20:26-07:00","id":1537249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537245#post1537245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of animals, humans included, actually have seemingly inborn notions of fairness that they react poorly to if they happen to be violated. Of course, if vampires are vampires and undead mockeries of life, then fuck 'em.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also directly contradicted by the fact that humans have a fantastic ability to create hereditary systems of hierarchy as well. A good argument is that human history can be summarized in four to three different economic systems.<br /> <br /> Tribalistic: Self-explanatory, built around collection of self-sustaining communities.<br /> <br /> Agrarian: Essentially when land became the commerce of humanity and everything revolved around the acquisition of either A:] More of it. B:] Humans to work it.<br /> <br /> Capitalist: When the primary pursuit of human wealth shifted from acquisition of land via the New World (which was a horrifying land grab that shook up economic systems across the globe) to the Acquisition of Wealth via other means. One could argue the Civil War and Russian Revolution were the last dying gasps of the Agrarian commerce system.<br /> <br /> Post-Capitalist: The question of whether sustainable capitalism, communism, socialism, or another system entirely can be created from the destructive tendencies of wealth hording.<br /> <br /> Vampires are stuck in Agrarian systems because even though they live in the Modern World, everything is about the acquisition and maintenance of Domain. Anarchs either want to go back to tribalist or replace the local rulership but have yet to offer a way for vampires to move to a Capitalist system. Vampire powers mean that the acquisition of non-land based wealth is inherently less valuable than territory with people living on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537247#post1537247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say a better definition would be as follows:<br /> <br /> Camarilla: Classical Fascism as defined by Mussolini as &quot;Everything inside the state, nothing outside the state, nothing above the state&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Hedonistic Blood Cult who believe themselves the heroes for fighting against the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: You're not my real parent, you can't tell me what to do.<br /> <br /> The problem with &quot;punk&quot; is that as a political viewpoint, it doesn't understand anything beyond itself. It is being counter to whatever the current mainstream accepts. Thus &quot;Punk&quot; can easily identify with whatever is fringe at the moment, thus why Traditionalist values were antithetical to punk back in the 80's and 90's and now with all the progressive stuff going on in society these days, wanting a traditional monogamous family unit is considered subversive by some.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's recited by punks but like most actually erudite criticisms, it comes from a much older source in Frank Wihoit. A composer of classical music and anti-segregationist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://slate.com/business/2022/06/wilhoits-law-conservatives-frank-wilhoit.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://compote.slate.com/images/505f6184-b5e8-4ee7-99b9-89c9af90bdf0.jpeg?width=1560&amp;rect=3420x2280&amp;offset=146x0\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://slate.com/business/2022/06/wilhoits-law-conservatives-frank-wilhoit.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Pithiest Critique of Modern Conservatism Keeps Getting Credited to the Wrong Man </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://slate.com/business/2022/06/wilhoits-law-conservatives-frank-wilhoit.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://slate.com/business/2022/06/wilhoits-law-conservatives-frank-wilhoit.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> &ldquo;Wilhoit&rsquo;s Law&rdquo; was coined by a different Frank Wilhoit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-12-2024, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T22:59:46-07:00","id":1537250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537248#post1537248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sigh, the core issue is what is considered &quot;fair&quot; rather than the existence of fairness being violated.<br /> <br /> Toss two people in a pit, put a knife in the center, state that whichever one is still alive by the end gets to leave.<br /> <br /> They start equidistant from the knife, they are both equally forced into the situation, they are both promised the same prize for achieving victory. That is pretty dang fair in the grand scheme of things, because people understand that bad situations happen and you just have to deal with them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the person who doesn't pay attention to the situation and starts complaining that it is unfair that they are forced to compete... is usually the one who gets stabbed by the one who doesn't have a problem with it. But this too is a fair outcome because the individuals had the freedom of choice for what they wanted to prioritize, their philosophical integrity or their continued survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire society created by elders wouldn't survive if elders actually let getting whacked slide, no matter what they thought of the vanquished. &quot;Fairness&quot; wouldn't enter directly into it; the traditions compel them in their politics, so they have to at least put on a front of unified strength against upstarts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I would be willing to bet that most animals that care about &quot;fairness&quot; are also domesticated, meaning their lives are sheltered from the harsher realities of existence. </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> Nope. It's not something that humans produced; they're the product of a socially-oriented selection process that promoted overall survival because the individuals cooperated instead of trying to find out which one would be the last one standing. Humans don't really know how to produce that kind of behavior via domestication, actually; domesticating a species pretty much just promotes neoteny and a needle-focused set of physical traits under human watch. Domesticated chickens are rather infamous for ganging up on human favorites, but that requires a far more traditional farm setup.<br /> <br /> Fairness also gets enforced by the participants in the social order. Chimps don't tend to suffer tyrants among their troops; as soon as an opposing political figure can stand up to them even a little, the terrorized members of a troupe will set upon the violator of fairness with terrible violence, sending them off with a multitude of deep bite marks and typically also with their balls squished out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T23:05:30-07:00","id":1537251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537244#post1537244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see this being a common perception, but it would be just as accurate to say that if an Elder got killed by a young upstart, clearly that Elder wasn't worth the blood they fed on. For every Elder that would mourn or try to avenge the death of their contemporary, there are several Elders who don't care one way or the other, and more than a few that breath a sigh of relief because the boons or old deals made are now no longer in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, generally speaking, the Elders of the Camarilla have a good reason for not wanting young vampires to feel like they can kill elders and get away with it. Maybe if a young vampire killed an elder in a particularly clever way, or if the elder was absolutely despised by everyone in the city, they might get away with a minor punishment. But I feel it's likely that even the deceased elder's former rivals and enemies would want the young vampire to be punished as severely as possible, if only to make a public point of what happens when vampires kill one another (specially old vampires like them). They might be glad their rival is deceased, but they also know that they could very well be the next one that gets killed by some youngster who doesn't believe he'll be punished. <br /> <br /> This is especially important when you consider diablere, and the fact that the only way for young vampires to get stronger is to kill older vampires. This means that every single older, lower generation vampire has a really, reallu good reason for wanting to see young vampires get punished for murdering elders, rather than risking having things turning into another open season like it was during the Anarch Revolts.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Camarilla is controlled by elder vampires, not younger ones, and they deliberately stack the deck and the rules in their own favor, pushing those who are young or lack power for breaking the rules, while avoiding similar punishments themselves. The elders of the Camarilla are mostly a bunch of asshole hypocrites, but that's just the nature of a punk-focused game like VtM - of course the people in charge are asshole hypocrites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T23:08:32-07:00","id":1537252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537249#post1537249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also directly contradicted by the fact that humans have a fantastic ability to create hereditary systems of hierarchy as well. A good argument is that human history can be summarized in four to three different economic systems.<br /> <br /> Tribalistic: Self-explanatory, built around collection of self-sustaining communities.<br /> <br /> Agrarian: Essentially when land became the commerce of humanity and everything revolved around the acquisition of either A:] More of it. B:] Humans to work it.<br /> <br /> Capitalist: When the primary pursuit of human wealth shifted from acquisition of land via the New World (which was a horrifying land grab that shook up economic systems across the globe) to the Acquisition of Wealth via other means. One could argue the Civil War and Russian Revolution were the last dying gasps of the Agrarian commerce system.<br /> <br /> Post-Capitalist: The question of whether sustainable capitalism, communism, socialism, or another system entirely can be created from the destructive tendencies of wealth hording.<br /> <br /> Vampires are stuck in Agrarian systems because even though they live in the Modern World, everything is about the acquisition and maintenance of Domain. Anarchs either want to go back to tribalist or replace the local rulership but have yet to offer a way for vampires to move to a Capitalist system. Vampire powers mean that the acquisition of non-land based wealth is inherently less valuable than territory with people living on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely an interesting take on it. Though my brain glitches trying to make it fit due to some of the mechanics involved or in some cases not involved.<br /> <br /> Vampires will mimic while in public the society and system of whatever the local kine are currently using. This has been one of my personal critiques of the setting since kindred vampires don't really have a society of their own. In the Blade setting they have their own standalone language, in the Anita Blake books the vampires have a lot of ceremony involved in proper behavior and gift giving when entering a domain rather than just saying hi, in the Priest movie the vampires had system more akin to a xenomorph hive, etc.<br /> <br /> Next the switch from Tribalistic to Agrarian is mechanically just a Coterie getting a defensible haven and a live in Herd of sufficient size. Once that is achieved, they build up supplies in case of emergency. Their population never unintentionally grows, and while they obviously can be killed, they never die of old age, thus the inheritance issue of the agrarian system never comes into play.<br /> <br /> I would argue that the vampires basically jump from Tribalistic to Agrarian to Post-Capitalistic since once their feeding and safety is secured, they focus their energy on either self-improvement (stat boosting) or alleviating boredom. But most of the fluff runs counter to this, often with no greater explanation than &quot;because reasons&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T23:23:51-07:00","id":1537253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527662-progressive-policies-are-pro-vampire?p=1537249#post1537249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also directly contradicted by the fact that humans have a fantastic ability to create hereditary systems of hierarchy as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. Those systems still require cooperation, so they can't get rid of all of the aversion to inequity. It's just that there's a group that tends to exclude non-members from its considerations of equity; it still sets up a game that's meant to be played by perceived equals. Upsets to the game are punished severely, especially if by a member of an out-group. This is the clash of two behaviors that we share with chimps - assaulting out-groups as an in-group and the aforementioned aversion to inequity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T10:48:43-07:00","id":1537265,"title":"","content":"I always went with the notion and stressed it to new players in our games is that elders have the mindset that they can do what they want, but do it in a way that it doesn't endanger there lofty perch that they fought tooth and claw over and the Prince isn't going to be all that sorry if a neonate gets punished severely for speaking out of turn or acting above there station. In fact they would be all for it until it stops being amusing or risks the masquerade then the Prince will come down like a hammer on all parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-12-2024, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}